So, I was having a great run last night with an Orcish Wizard.  (I made 
a post about it yesterday, asking for help.)  Being new, I was pleased 
that I seemed to have a good character.

I died in the most stupid newbie-ish way possible.  For those who 
haven't read my other post (where I described everything that happened 
to me, just prior to the death.) I'll give a Reader's Digest version of 
what happened:

I got lucky, got Telepathy early along with a blindfold.  Was using that 
to scope out monsters and movement.  However, being new, I decided to 
explore the dungeon with the blindfold on.  I ended up falling in a pit. 
  Well, as long as I learn from the mistake, it's okay.  So, I'm on a 
hostile level, separated from my pet.

So, as I'm looking for the stairs to get back up, I come across a group 
of 4 or so Orcs.  These guys are way too tough for me without my pet, so 
they're beating me senseless.  Finally, in desperation, I read a scroll 
of teleportation and I end up not too far from the stairs.  I 
congratulate myself for thinking of that, and climb up to the level my 
pet is on, and I'm reunited with my cat.  Now I feel like I can 
definately take on anything.  I have a bunch of scrolls (one 
unidentified one turned out to be a scroll of genocide), potions, and 
wands.  I feel totally ready to go deeper in the dungeons than ever 
before.  (Keep in mind, this would be dlvl 7.  I'm not too good at this 
game yet.  For reference, I was on dlvl 5 at this point.)  I'm exploring 
the last bits of the level I'm on, when I come across a kitten.  Now, 
I'm pretty weak still so I decide to let my pet take out the kitten.

Because I was full of myself and not paying attention, I thought my cat 
was fighting the kitten (and vice versa).  It turns out the kitten was 
attacking me and my cat was attacking the kitten.  So, the kitten killed 
me because I was being stupid.  I was really, really upset at myself 
after that.

(But it's all okay... a few hours later I made it to dlvl 8 with a Monk, 
and died in combat with a Mumak.  It was, without a doubt, my best game 
ever.  It was fairly easy, too.  I think Monk just became my favorite 
